[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/corposant-lightning.png" id="3_icon"]

; Corposant (scripts/Corposant.cs), 2026-11-09: sailors' word for St Elmo's fire. A ball of storm-fire loosed in a random
; direction that bounces off the edges of the camera's view for a few seconds, striking everything it passes. Pure
; Lightning, one of the thin elements. Nobody's opener; everyone earns it with the Storm Petrel feat (Lightning kills in
; one run). TargetingMode 7 is Unaimed - it picks no target, spot or direction - and DamageShape 1 a projectile.
;
; BaseDamage is ONE STRIKE of one ball on one body; a ball strikes the same body at most every half second
; (Corposant.StrikeEvery). BaseCooldown is the cast (the ONE fire loop). BaseProjectileCount is the balls a cast looses
; (plus Amount). The ball's life is Corposant.BaseLifeSeconds (3 s) plus the ZoneDuration lines here (Effect 13); the
; card says it as "Duration +17%", never in seconds. No range: the edges of the view are its range.
;
; FIRST GUESSES, untuned. Spells start small (Eric, 2026-11-02): one ball at level 1, two at 3, three at 6, so about one
; ball out at level 1 and four or five at level 8 (3 balls x 4 s over 2.6 s). Written out in full so
; Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own (ScalingTagsMask 8211: Damage, Cooldown, ProjectileCount,
; Duration): every level adds damage and even levels shorten the cast by 0.1 s. Level 8: 15 a strike, three balls every
; 2.6 s, each burning 4 s.

